<%#
  views/editor/comments.ejs

  The editor's comment moderation page: every comment on the site, newest first, with
  the article it was posted on, a search box (comment text or author name) and pages of
  20. Each row can be edited in place or deleted after a confirmation.

  The page is sent as an empty frame: the table body starts empty, and
  public/js/editor/comments.js fills it from GET /api/comments and does every edit
  and delete with Ajax, so the page never reloads. Building the rows in one place (the
  script) means the first page and every later page look exactly the same.
  The element ids below are what that script uses.

  Rendered by: controllers/commentController.js (showCommentModerationPage), for
  GET /editor/comments. Only editors get here: the route uses requireRole('editor').
  Locals: title (the page title); currentUser comes from middleware/setCurrentUser.js
  and is read by the shared header.
  Includes: the shared head, header and footer (views/partials) and the editor nav (SM).
  Owner: OS.
%>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<%- include('../partials/head', { title: title }) %>

<body class="page-container">
  <%- include('../partials/header') %>
  <%- include('partials/editorNav', { activePage: 'comments' }) %>

  <main class="main-content" id="comment-moderation">
    <h2>Comments</h2>

    <%#
      role="search" tells screen readers this form filters the list below.
      The script searches while the editor types; it also stops Enter from submitting
      the form, which would reload the page.
    %>
    <form id="comment-search-form" class="card" role="search">
      <label for="comment-search">Search comments or author names</label>
      <%# maxlength matches the server's search limit (100 characters). %>
      <input type="search" id="comment-search" name="search" class="form-field"
        maxlength="100" placeholder="Part of a comment or a name..." autocomplete="off">
    </form>

    <%#
      Loading and "no comments" messages appear here.
      aria-live="polite" makes screen readers announce the new text when it changes.
    %>
    <p id="comment-list-status" class="loading" aria-live="polite">Loading comments...</p>
    <%# Errors from the server, for example an edit with empty text. role="alert" is announced at once. %>
    <p id="comment-list-error" class="form-error" role="alert" hidden></p>

    <%#
      On a narrow screen the table scrolls sideways inside this box, not the whole page
      (requirements: responsive for computer, tablet and phone). table-scroll is the
      shared class for this in public/css/main.css (SH), so every table on the site
      behaves the same way.
    %>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Comment</th>
            <th scope="col">Author</th>
            <th scope="col">Article</th>
            <th scope="col">Posted</th>
            <th scope="col">Actions</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody id="comment-rows"></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <nav id="pagination" aria-label="Pages of comments">
      <button type="button" id="previous-page" class="btn" disabled>Previous</button>
      <span id="page-info"></span>
      <button type="button" id="next-page" class="btn" disabled>Next</button>
    </nav>

    <noscript>
      <p class="form-error">Comment moderation needs JavaScript. Please turn it on.</p>
    </noscript>
  </main>

  <%- include('../partials/footer') %>

  <%# apiClient first: public/js/editor/comments.js uses it. %>
  <script src="/js/shared/apiClient.js"></script>
  <script src="/js/editor/comments.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
